---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to send corrections and additions to the Tioman climbing guidebook — a pull request, or an email to Ri Zhao."
  section="/contribute"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/#areas">Guidebook</a><span>/</span><span>Contribute</span>
    </nav>

    <section>
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Corrections &amp; contributions</h2>
        <p>
          Much of this is transcribed from weathered handwriting, and assembled with the help of
          AI. Errors are likely. Please help fix them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="two-col">
        <div style="display:grid;gap:1.25rem">
          <div class="panel">
            <span class="label">Two ways in</span>
            <h3>Send a change</h3>
            <p>
              <strong>1. Open a pull request.</strong> The whole guidebook — text, route data, this
              site — lives in one public repository. Edit the source and propose the change directly.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href="https://github.com/therizhao/tioman-climbing"
                >github.com/therizhao/tioman-climbing</a
              >
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>2. Or just email Ri Zhao.</strong> Describe what's wrong and what it should
              say — a corrected grade, a missing route, a name, a photo you'd like credited or
              removed.
            </p>
            <p><a href="mailto:rizhaow@gmail.com">rizhaow@gmail.com</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="panel">
            <span class="label">Generated with AI — check our work</span>
            <h3>Hallucinations happen</h3>
            <p>
              This guidebook was compiled and drafted with the help of AI tools working from scans
              of a handwritten logbook. That means <strong
                >plausible-looking mistakes can slip in</strong
              > — a grade that was never given, a name spelled wrong, a pitch invented from an
              ambiguous sketch.
            </p>
            <p>
              If something looks off, it may well be. Please flag it by either route above — every
              correction from someone who has actually been there makes this more trustworthy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <span class="label">Known gaps</span>
          <h3>Help us close these</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Muka</strong> (7a+, 360&nbsp;m) has a heading in the record but no topo anywhere</li>
            <li><strong>Beckwith–Traver</strong> is dated both 2009 and 2011 in the same document</li>
            <li>
              "Blood Sweat and <em>Fear</em>" or "<em>Tears</em>"? The map and the route page disagree
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Damai Sentosa</strong> pitch grades come from a pencil sketch — approximate
            </li>
            <li>The <strong>Puncak Nipah</strong> sport list is read off a weathered painted board</li>
            <li>The <strong>North Tower via ferrata</strong> — length, grade and access details</li>
            <li>Several first ascensionists are recorded only by first name</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
